<figure class="fig-tight">
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 220 262" role="img" aria-label="Fig P04.1 — al-Khwārizmī's gnomon: the x² square, two 5x strips, and the missing 25 corner close into (x + 5)²">
<rect x="20" y="150" width="90" height="90" fill="#dce8f7" stroke="#3574d4" stroke-width="2"/>
<rect x="110" y="150" width="75" height="90" fill="#eef3fa" stroke="#3574d4" stroke-width="2"/>
<rect x="20" y="75" width="90" height="75" fill="#eef3fa" stroke="#3574d4" stroke-width="2"/>
<rect x="110" y="75" width="75" height="75" fill="none" stroke="#c25b4a" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 4"/>
<text x="65" y="200" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" fill="#3a4a5e">x²</text>
<text x="147" y="200" font-size="12.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#3a4a5e">5x</text>
<text x="65" y="116" font-size="12.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#3a4a5e">5x</text>
<text x="147" y="116" font-size="12.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c25b4a">25</text>
<text x="65" y="256" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">x</text>
<text x="147" y="256" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">5</text>
<text x="65" y="68" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">x</text>
<text x="8" y="116" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">5</text>
</svg>
<figcaption><strong>Fig P04.1.</strong> al-Khwārizmī's own drawing: the \(x^2\) square with two \(5 \times x\) strips on its east and north edges — one \(5 \times 5 = 25\) corner short of the bigger square \((x + 5)^2\). Pay for the corner and the gnomon closes: \(x^2 + 10x + 25 = (x + 5)^2\).</figcaption>
</figure>
